From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 10:49:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: Describe axi_daisy without the
 test-only note

The axi_daisy description called the switch test only and put its
default inside the power-up note. State the values first and give the
default in its own parentheses, so a later change of the default only
has to touch that one marker.

No change in behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
index 1003f248a72..d19256d46ca 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-pm.c
@@ -358,7 +358,7 @@ void avd_pm_apply_axi_tunables(struct avd_dev *avd)
 static unsigned int axi_daisy;
 module_param(axi_daisy, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(axi_daisy,
-		 "Test only: T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (read at each decoder power-up, default 0)");
+		 "T8132 bridge as macOS's Daisy, read at each decoder power-up: 0 off, 1 log only, 2 read, 3 program (default 0)");
 
 static const struct avd_tunable avd_daisy_flow_up[] = {
 	{ 0x0000, 0x800000ff, 0x80000026 }, /* UP_CMD_CREDIT_GS_ALLOC */
-- 
